stitures of $17 million, reflecting organic growth across all segments and most major geographic regions, with organic growth in the U.S. and western Europe more than offsetting organic declines in the emerging markets.","context":"Executive Summary","section":"Key Performance Indicators and Non-GAAP Measures","block":373,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001524472-26-000012","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001524472","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1524472/000152447226000012/xyl-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/95a2807d635c338325f7e9964e1063075f1a52c7182e2fe921aa0f56874b1904.bin","sha256":"95a2807d635c338325f7e9964e1063075f1a52c7182e2fe921aa0f56874b1904"}},{"id":"7efdcfa36ede113ffd15240fd45f5ce3ca696384e8aa3fe9fd7d523fb10eda35","quote":"Operating income for 2025 was $1,223 million, reflecting an increase of $214 million, or 21.2%, compared to $1,009 million in 2024. Operating margin was 13.5% in 2025, up 170 basis points from 11.8% in 2024. The operating margin increase included negative impacts from increases in restructuring and realignment costs of $42 million and purchased intangible amortization of $4 million, partially offset by a decrease in special charges of $21 million. Excluding the impact of these items, adjusted operating income was $1,612 million, with an adjusted operating margin of 17.8% in 2025 as compared to adjusted operating income of $1,373 million with an adjusted operating margin of 16.0% in 2024, an increase of 180 basis points.","context":"Xylem reported revenue of $9,035 million for 2025, an increase of $473 million, or 5.5%, from $8,562 million reported in 2024. The increase consists of organic growth of $419 million and favorable foreign currency impacts of $71 million, partially offset by net revenue declines from acquisitions and divestitures of $17 million, reflecting organic growth across all segments and most major geographic regions, with organic growth in the U.S. and western Europe more than offsetting organic declines in the emerging markets.","section":"Key Performance Indicators and Non-GAAP Measures","block":374,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001524472-26-000012","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001524472","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1524472/000152447226000012/xyl-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/95a2807d635c338325f7e9964e1063075f1a52c7182e2fe921aa0f56874b1904.bin","sha256":"95a2807d635c338325f7e9964e1063075f1a52c7182e2fe921aa0f56874b1904"}},{"id":"9b706db5f7842d4f5cc65783d38c0085e195545dc40ac3f578e928cb24acdf8a","quote":"Additional financial highlights for 2025 include the following:","context":"Operating income for 2025 was $1,223 million, reflecting an increase of $214 million, or 21.2%, compared to $1,009 million in 2024. Operating margin was 13.5% in 2025, up 170 basis points from 11.8% in 2024. The operating margin increase included negative impacts from increases in restructuring and realignment costs of $42 million and purchased intangible amortization of $4 million, partially offset by a decrease in special charges of $21 million. Excluding the impact of these items, adjusted operating income was $1,612 million, with an adjusted operating margin of 17.8% in 2025 as compared to adjusted operating income of $1,373 million with an adjusted operating margin of 16.0% in 2024, an increase of 180 basis points.","section":"Key Performance Indicators and Non-GAAP Measures","block":375,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001524472-26-000012","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001524472","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1524472/0001524472260